  },
  "assumptions": [
    "Applies the published four-week discount quote to a synthetic D-day bill that matures exactly at the next calendar month end. August uses 31 days. A four-week instrument is not a verified 31-day CUSIP.",
    "Uses only the last valid quote on or before the preceding month end, with no future-yield input; weekends are covered by that last business-day quote.",
    "No intra-month mark-to-market, maturity-selection, realized rollover, accrued-cash or actual GBOM index path is observed; the official index return can differ.",
    "The alternative uses the one-month investment-basis yield and ACT/365 to make quote-convention sensitivity visible. It is not averaged into the primary estimate.",
    "January-July errors are a diagnostic, not an August confidence interval. No fitted bias correction is applied."
  ],
